Z||000000||underdog||04-24-2001||03:41 AM||||ok where to start? well hi everyone, nice to meet you all<P><BR>first off, is there anything else necessary for these springs to lower your car, or just put them on and you are an inch lower?<P>"The Fiero Store sells top quality Eibach lowering spring packages for 84-87 Fieros. Eibach springs will greatly improve handling with stiffer springs that lower your Fiero approximately 1" from factory ride height. The sport springs also enhance the beauty of the car by reducing excess wheel well space common to stock Fieros. Upgrade your springs today for maximum cornering speed. CHECK OUT THE TOOLS PAGE TO MAKE THE JOB EASIER!" they are from the "fiero store"<P>secondly, i am going to put a larger engine in my car, but i need it to be part way affordable. i live in canada so any canadians with suggestions and prices of a faster car, please tell me<P>lastly, did anyone elses 1986 fiero gt's spoiler fade really bad, i bought mine and it was faded bad, is this a consistant thing or will simply painting over it cure it?<P>thanks a million guys||||reg||7
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||04-24-2001||05:07 AM||||Welcome to the Forum!<P>First off the Eibach springs are simply installed and it will lower your Fiero, though it hasn't kept some from getting out the sawsall to get lower...<P>You want to go to a larger engine but how far do you want to go? Bigger than 2.8 could be 3.4, 3.4 DOHC, 3800, 3800 Supercharged, 4.6 Cadillac Northstar, 4.9 Cadillac V8 or 5.7 Chevy SB V8 (to name JUST a few of the engines that have been discussed!)?<P>Oxidizing paint is common with Fieros. <P>Using the "Search" option should give you most of the details of your questions! There are just bunches and bunches of posts about everything you just asked!||||reg||14
Z||000002||underdog||04-24-2001||05:49 AM||||ya thanks man, i just hate searching through the posts, half of them arent even what you asked for<P>thanks though, as for the engine, something like a supercharged 3.8 or a small block v-8 would be great, something not very expensive anyways<P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||04-24-2001||08:27 AM||||Replacement engine for a Fiero does not equal inexpensive.  A questionable junkyard engine is not worth the expense of the install.  A new crate engine is expensive to start with.<P>Wolter's Law: If you have the time, you won't have the money, if you have the money, you won't have the time.||||reg||7
Z||000004||Lore||04-24-2001||09:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B><P>Wolter's Law: If you have the time, you won't have the money, if you have the money, you won't have the time.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Damnit if that ain't the truth.  I got about $3000 and was just about ready to go off on my Fiero but now come to find out, my ship is leaving for 6 months!  I won't get back until January! (Navy)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Lore<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||04-24-2001||10:55 AM||||I used the Fiero Store Eibach's My car actually lowered 1.5" Once everything settled in. <P>The engine swaps are many. Doing the swap yourself saves lots of money. The easiest would be the 3.1 or 3.4 engines since they are basically a drop-in swap. Anything bigger (3800, V-8's, 3.4 dual overhead cam, etc) requires more work. It all comes down to How fast? How much?<P>"....Speed is just a question of money,<BR>How fast do you want to go?"<P>As for the fading, it is common on 12-17 year old cars. If the decklid isn't faded a body shop can match the paint and repaint just the wing. (All depends on the rest of the car)||||reg||1
Z||000006||underdog||04-24-2001||01:24 PM||||thanks again. and one last question, to the people with 18s on your car, no problems or anything?||||reg||5
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||04-24-2001||01:57 PM||||The fun part about 18s beside the price of tires is that once you have find a wheel with the righ offsets, you will have to be hypervigilant about potholes, rocks, nickels (okay maybe not nickels but you get the point.) to keep from denting the hell out of your very expensive wheels! <P>You would have a great look 18s or even 17 but man, you are vulnerable!||||reg||14
